{"nodes": [{"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_batch_card", "label": "Batch Card (candidate C3)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "Fingerprint under test", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Triage unit changes from one submission to the batch it belongs to, persisted as a record; family inform+prevent. It deliberately refuses to judge one item's authorship so the maintainer never has to accuse an individual (a direct answer to the 20.8% ban/block countermeasure). Pitch must lead with '9 accounts, 40 repos, 6 hours' rather than 'AI slop detection', or a judge files it with the fourteen 2026 slop-* repos."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_batch_record_unit", "label": "Cross-install submission index and persisted batch record", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "The unit nothing else occupies: a batch record spanning multiple accounts across installations. Every competitor scores either the single submission or the single author's history, so none can say the sentence '9 accounts'. This is the only part a judge needs to credit, and the bucket 'already indexes submissions across repositories into campaign records' came back empty."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_prt_scan_campaign", "label": "prt-scan campaign \u2014 Six Accounts, One Actor (Wiz Research)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "THE CRUX", "source_url": "https://www.wiz.io/blog/six-accounts-one-actor-inside-the-prt-scan-supply-chain-campaign", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "Rami McCarthy, Hila Ramati, Scott Piper, Benjamin Read", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Single most important finding in the scan: Wiz linked six accounts post-hoc by identical branch naming prt-scan-{12-hex}, uniform PR title/body, Proton Mail +N variants and timing clusters \u2014 precisely the idea's structural tells and minhash, done three weeks later for a blog rather than at triage time. The 2026-03-11 to 2026-04-03 window is a ready-made publicly documented replayable ground-truth batch."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_kai_gritun_reputation_farming", "label": "Kai Gritun reputation farming (Socket via InfoWorld)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "Evidence FOR coordinated multi-account campaigns", "source_url": "https://www.infoworld.com/article/4132851/open-source-maintainers-are-being-targeted-by-ai-agent-as-part-of-reputation-farming.html", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "103 PRs across 95 repositories within days of profile creation, linked to the OpenClaw agent platform. Caveat the scan insists on reporting: ONE account across 95 repos is cross-repo burst (signal ii) but not multi-account batching (signal i)."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_github_open_pr_cap", "label": "GitHub open-PR cap for contributors without write access", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: platform", "source_url": "https://www.coderabbit.ai/blog/github-gives-maintainers-a-throttle-for-the-ai-pull-request", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Strongest competitor in the whole scan and it fails on the exact axis the idea owns: the cap is per-contributor, per-repository, so 9 accounts x 40 repos x 3 open PRs = up to 1,080 fully compliant PRs. Rebuttal to prepare: the cap controls volume per person, the batch card restores the shape. Shipped date 2026-06-17 rests on CodeRabbit's secondary account; the github.blog changelog entry was NOT confirmed from primary source."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_github_abuse_spam_reporting", "label": "GitHub abuse/spam reporting", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "What GitHub actually ships", "source_url": "https://docs.github.com/en/communities/maintaining-your-safety-on-github/reporting-abuse-or-spam", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Per item, one at a time, nothing aggregates \u2014 so no GitHub surface tells a maintainer 'this is one of 112 submissions by 9 accounts across 40 repos'."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_github_triage_tools_under_consideration", "label": "GitHub triage tools under consideration (not shipped)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "Under consideration, not shipped", "source_url": "https://www.theregister.com/2026/02/03/github_kill_switch_pull_requests_ai/", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Main platform risk: GitHub PM Camilla Moraes lists 'triage tools, possibly AI-based' among options investigated, and GitHub has all the cross-install data by default \u2014 if GitHub shipped a batch view the idea is absorbed. PM Matthew Isabel's 'we don't think counting AI-generated PRs is the right metric' is an argument FOR the framing: the batch card counts the batch, not AI PRs. A 20-hour build cannot out-data GitHub, only out-frame it."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_arxiv_2609_07542_ai_policies", "label": "arXiv 2609.07542 \u2014 Landscape of AI Policies in Popular Open Source Projects", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: research", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.07542", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "Andre Hora, Romain Robbes, Stefano Zacchiroli", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "281 policies across 2,000 repos; countermeasure taxonomy entirely per-item or per-user (Close PR 48.4%, Ban/block user 20.8%, Label the PR 2.1%, Limit number of PRs 1.6%, Stop accepting PRs 1.6%). No discussion of coordinated campaigns, multi-account operators, batches or shared cross-project indices. The 2.1% label figure is mildly bad news for a label-writing mechanism and should shape the demo toward the comment and the record, not the label."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_greptile", "label": "Greptile", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: startup", "source_url": "https://www.greptile.com/docs/introduction", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Analyzes each PR against a graph of its own repository in ~3 minutes. No cross-repository or cross-customer analysis, no author history, no spam detection, no multi-account correlation \u2014 single PR vs its own repo's codebase."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_coderabbit", "label": "CodeRabbit", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: startup", "source_url": "https://www.coderabbit.ai/blog/github-gives-maintainers-a-throttle-for-the-ai-pull-request", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Per-PR AI review. Campaign detection: no evidence either way \u2014 the page opened is CodeRabbit commentary on GitHub's cap, so its own cross-repo capability is logged as not established."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_scanaislop", "label": "scanaislop / aislop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: startup", "source_url": "https://scanaislop.com/blog/ai-slop-open-source-maintainer-policy/", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Deterministic CI gate, 50+ rules, no LLM at runtime; scores the single submission. Notable: it states it is 'not an authorship detector' \u2014 the same disavowal this idea makes, but applied to code patterns rather than to batches."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_connectory_ai", "label": "connectory.ai", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: startup", "source_url": "https://www.connectory.ai/solutions/open-source/", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "'Free AI Code Review for Open Source, AI Slop Detection' \u2014 NOT OPENED, search-result title only. Logged as a LEAD."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_socket", "label": "Socket", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: startup / VERDICT", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Biggest unchecked risk in the scan: Socket published the reputation-farming research and clearly holds cross-ecosystem data, but no Socket product page was opened, so whether they ship a maintainer-facing batch view is unknown. Worth one lookup before the build."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_open_slop", "label": "dr-alberto/open-slop", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "The two closest matches in all of OSS", "source_url": "https://github.com/marketplace/actions/open-slop", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "dr-alberto", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Closest OSS match. Three signals \u2014 Velocity, Shotgun ('15 PRs in 15 unrelated repositories'), Ghost (account age) \u2014 and its own docs say it analyses 'single PR behavior and account history, not coordinated campaigns'. Wedge: it owns signal (ii) only, holds one account in memory, has no cross-install index of submission text, no shared structural tells between different authors, no persisted batch record, and still implicitly judges the individual. FORK VERDICT: MECHANISM, do NOT fork \u2014 signal (ii) is ~40 lines against the events API and forking makes the submission a reskin. Concede it on stage: open-slop asks 'is this person spraying?', this asks 'is this submission one of many, from many?'."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_contributor_summary", "label": "kurehajime/contributor-summary", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "The two closest matches in all of OSS", "source_url": "https://github.com/kurehajime/contributor-summary", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "kurehajime", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Per-author cross-repo activity summary ('Spot AI slop. Stop the flood.'), 35 KB, no licence, 0 stars. Same per-author axis as open-slop, even thinner. FORK VERDICT: MECHANISM, do NOT fork \u2014 same axis, same reskin risk."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_pr_slop", "label": "visrutsuresh/PR-slop", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "The two closest matches in all of OSS", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "visrutsuresh", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Closest thing to batch triage as a UI concept: takes a queue of open PRs and returns three piles (read first, read next, likely to be closed). But it sorts one repo's queue by per-item score, never discovers that items belong together, and never looks outside the repo. No licence \u2014 unusable as a fork base for that reason alone."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_slop_guard_nkasi_e", "label": "Nkasi-e/slop-guard", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": "https://github.com/Nkasi-e/slop-guard", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "Nkasi-e", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Rust, MIT, 4 stars \u2014 highest-starred of the 14 GitHub 'ai slop pull request' results. Unit: single diff, pre-PR."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_pr_slop_filter", "label": "Noxlie/pr-slop-filter", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "Noxlie", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "TypeScript, MIT, 3-layer analysis of a single PR."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_deslop_kitten", "label": "dorcha-inc/deslop-kitten", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "dorcha-inc", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Go, MIT GitHub Action that flags AI slop PRs before review. Unit: single PR."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_turingmerge", "label": "makalin/turingmerge", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "makalin", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Net Code Survival Rate to distinguish human effort from AI copy-paste. Unit: single PR, post-hoc."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_cleanoss", "label": "Bardemic/cleanOSS", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "Bardemic", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Auto-detect AI PRs and block repeat slop-offenders \u2014 single PR plus per-author repeat memory. No licence."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_slopguard_kero168", "label": "kero168/slopguard", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "kero168", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Signal-based triage for AI-generated PRs, Action and CLI. Unit: single PR."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_slop_sheriff", "label": "frostney/slop-sheriff", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "frostney", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "'Cowboy code reviewer' with focused lanes and evidence-backed findings. Unit: single PR. No licence."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_characterizing_ai_slop", "label": "Characterizing-AI-slop \u2014 What Makes a Pull Request AI Slop?", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss / research", "source_url": "https://github.com/sepehr-rs/Characterizing-AI-slop", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "sepehr-rs", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Empirical study of maintainer labels on single PRs, CC-BY-4.0. Groups individually, not into campaigns. Repo opened via API; paper not read."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_single_submission_slop_scorers", "label": "Single-submission slop scorer cohort (fourteen 2026 slop-* repos)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: oss / FORK-BASE BUCKETS", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Fourteen repos named slop-*, all created in 2026, none above 4 stars, none forked \u2014 the signature of an idea everyone has had, and the real hazard is fashion, not any one competitor. FORK VERDICT: do NOT fork, and for a stronger reason than licence \u2014 they do the exact thing this idea refuses to do (judge one item's authorship), so importing one would contradict the pitch on stage. A thesis question, not a licence question."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_probot", "label": "Probot / create-probot-app", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS \u2014 PLUMBING", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "probot", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "PLUMBING, fork with pure upside: webhook routing, App auth, JWT/installation token handling \u2014 roughly 6 of the 20 hours gone for free. Licence/last-push unverified this run (the probot template API query returned a corrupted record)."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_octokit", "label": "Octokit (octokit.js, webhooks.js)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS \u2014 PLUMBING", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": "octokit", "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "PLUMBING, fork freely: typed webhook payloads, pagination, and the public events API pager that produces the cross-repo burst profile without any App install."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_minhash_lsh_library", "label": "minhash/LSH library (datasketch, murmurhash3)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS \u2014 PLUMBING", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "PLUMBING, fork freely: gives signal (i) \u2014 near-duplicate submission text across accounts \u2014 in an afternoon rather than two days."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_fork_base_plumbing_bucket", "label": "Fork-base verdict: PLUMBING, fork freely (S1A)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Probot, Octokit, a minhash/LSH library and any label/comment writer: forking all of this is invisible to a judge and leaves 100% of the idea intact."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_fork_base_mechanism_bucket", "label": "Fork-base verdict: MECHANISM, do NOT fork (S1A)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "FORK-BASE BUCKETS", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "open-slop and contributor-summary hand over the author cross-repo burst signal pre-built \u2014 the one signal that already reads to a judge as 'swarm detection' \u2014 so reskinning either leaves the builder credit for only the index. The third bucket, 'already indexes submissions across repositories into campaign records', is empty."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_cold_start_public_seed", "label": "Cold-start seeding from public event data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "Build consequence worth flagging", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "The cross-install index is worthless with one installation, so for a 20-hour demo it must be seeded from public data (GH Archive / public events API over a known window) rather than requiring installs. Single most useful operational finding in the scan."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_auto_close_on_silence_policy", "label": "Auto-close-on-silence policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: workaround", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Closest existing workaround to the idea's maintainer-set rule: PRs labelled 'maybe automated' and closed after 1 day unless a human responds. It is a per-item timer, not a batch rule. Source is a search summary \u2014 LEAD."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_turso_bounty_retirement", "label": "Turso bug-bounty retirement", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: workaround", "source_url": "https://dev.to/ritabratamaiti/ai-slop-killed-the-open-source-bug-bounty-2o64", "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Turso retired its $1,000-per-bug bounty after AI-generated submissions overwhelmed maintainers \u2014 the curl pattern spreading: the incentive is removed because the triage cost cannot be paid."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_ai_ddos_study", "label": "AI Slop Is DDoSing Open Source study (AI-DDoS)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: research", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "294 repositories and >2M PRs and issues; coins AI-DDoS; merge rates fell 18.18% for first-time contributors while volume rose. Measures the flood in aggregate and does not decompose it into operators."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_arxiv_2604_19965_security_prs", "label": "arXiv 2604.19965 \u2014 Insights into Security-Related AI-Generated Pull Requests", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: research", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "675 AI-generated security PRs; AI patches repeat a narrow set of weaknesses. Obliquely relevant because repetition across submissions is the idea's structural tell, but it scores PRs one at a time. Search-summary only \u2014 LEAD."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_arxiv_2509_14745_agentic_coding", "label": "arXiv 2509.14745 \u2014 On the Use of Agentic Coding", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: research", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "567 Claude Code PRs across 157 projects, scored individually. LEAD."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_arxiv_2603_26487_to_ban_or_not", "label": "arXiv 2603.26487 \u2014 To Ban or not to Ban? How Open Source Projects Govern GenAI Contributions", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swarm-dynamics/competitors-S1A.md", "source_location": "CLASS: research", "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-10-02", "author": null, "contributor": "Subagent C", "rationale": "Governance, per project. LEAD."}, {"id": "hackathon_idea_ai_swarm_dynamics_competitors_s1a_prompt_question_shield", "label": "Prompt+Question Shield (Apart Research winner)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "hackathon-idea/ai-swar